{#
    Static top-level nav, above Sylius's category menu. Hooked in via
    config/packages/twig_hooks.yaml.

    Desktop (lg+): the page links and the Request a Quote button in one row.
    Phones/tablets: the links don't fit in a row, so they live in the
    hamburger slide-out instead (see bundles/SyliusShopBundle/.../navbar/
    menu.html.twig), and this row is just a full-width Request a Quote
    button -- the site's main call to action.

    Matches the live site's nav (Home, Services, Shop, About, Contact,
    Request a Quote) minus "Shop": the product categories show in their
    own menu row instead.
#}
<div class="w-100 border-bottom">
    <nav class="navbar p-0 justify-content-center d-none d-lg-flex" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <div class="navbar-nav flex-row gap-3 py-2 align-items-center">
            <a class="nav-link" href="{{ path('sylius_shop_homepage') }}">Home</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="{{ path('app_shop_services') }}">Services</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="{{ path('app_shop_about') }}">About</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="{{ path('app_shop_contact') }}">Contact</a>
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" href="{{ path('app_shop_rfq') }}">Request a Quote</a>
        </div>
    </nav>
    <div class="d-lg-none px-3 py-2">
        <a class="btn btn-primary w-100" href="{{ path('app_shop_rfq') }}">Request a Quote</a>
    </div>
</div>
